// Wires together all Trust Codegen crates into a single entry point:
//   trust_ir -> ISel -> Optimization -> RegAlloc -> Frame Lowering -> Encoding -> Mach-O

//! End-to-end compilation pipeline for Trust Codegen.
//!
//! Takes a trust_ir function (represented as `trust_cg_lower::Function`) and produces
//! a valid AArch64 Mach-O .o file.
//!
//! # Pipeline phases
//!
//! ```text
//! Phase 1: ISel (trust-cg-lower)
//!   trust_cg_lower::Function -> trust_cg_lower::isel::ISelFunction
//!   (VRegs, canonical trust_cg_ir::AArch64Opcode — unified in issue #73)
//!
//! Phase 2: Adapt ISel -> IR (structural only — opcodes are already unified)
//!   trust_cg_lower::isel::ISelFunction -> trust_cg_ir::MachFunction
//!
//! Phase 3: Optimization (trust-cg-opt)
//!   trust_cg_ir::MachFunction -> trust_cg_ir::MachFunction (optimized)
//!
//! Phase 4: Adapt IR -> RegAlloc
//!   trust_cg_ir::MachFunction -> trust_cg_regalloc::RegAllocFunction
//!
//! Phase 5: Register Allocation (trust-cg-regalloc)
//!   trust_cg_regalloc::RegAllocFunction -> AllocationResult (VReg -> PReg map)
//!
//! Phase 6: Apply allocation to IR
//!   trust_cg_ir::MachFunction + AllocationResult -> trust_cg_ir::MachFunction (PRegs only)
//!
//! Phase 7: Frame Lowering (trust-cg-codegen/frame)
//!   Insert prologue/epilogue, eliminate frame indices
//!
//! Phase 8: Encoding (trust-cg-codegen/aarch64)
//!   trust_cg_ir::MachFunction -> Vec<u8> (machine code bytes)
//!
//! Phase 9: Mach-O Emission (trust-cg-codegen/macho)
//!   Vec<u8> -> Mach-O .o file bytes
//! ```
//!
//! # Type adapters and unification status (issue #73)
//!
//! **Unified (no adapter needed):**
//! - `AArch64Opcode`: ISel uses `trust_cg_ir::AArch64Opcode` directly.
//! - `InstFlags`: regalloc re-exports `trust_cg_ir::InstFlags` directly.
//! - `MachBlock` / `RegAllocBlock`: structurally identical after `loop_depth`
//!   was added to `trust_cg_ir::MachBlock`. Converted via `From<&MachBlock>`.
//! - `StackSlot` / `RegAllocStackSlot`: converted via `From<&StackSlot>`.
//! - Primitive types: `VReg`, `PReg`, `RegClass`, `BlockId`, `InstId`,
//!   `StackSlotId` — all re-exported from `trust_cg_ir` by regalloc.
//!
//! **Remaining structural adapters (separate types, with From/TryFrom impls):**
//! - `ISelOperand` / `RegAllocOperand`: ISel has `CondCode`/`Symbol`/`StackSlot(u32)`
//!   variants; regalloc omits `MemOp`/`FrameIndex`/`Special`.
//!   `TryFrom<&MachOperand>` for `RegAllocOperand` handles the conversion.
//! - `ISelInst` / `RegAllocInst`: regalloc separates defs/uses for liveness analysis;
//!   ISel has no flags/implicit-defs/proofs. Unification requires adding
//!   def/use classification to `trust_cg_ir::MachInst`.
//! - `ISelBlock`: ISel uses inline `Vec<ISelInst>` (not arena-indexed).
//! - `ISelFunction` / `RegAllocFunction`: ISel uses `HashMap<Block, ISelBlock>`
//!   (construction-friendly); regalloc uses `HashMap<StackSlotId, RegAllocStackSlot>`
//!   + `next_stack_slot`.
//!
//! The canonical types are in `trust_cg_ir`: `MachFunction`, `MachInst`, `MachBlock`,
//! `MachOperand`. ISel and regalloc types have been renamed to avoid confusion.
//! See `trust_cg_ir::type_hierarchy` for complete documentation.
//! See issue #73 for the remaining unification plan.

